<Shell Title="Privacy">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>This is a demo application. All invoices and payments in it are synthetic.</p>
    <h2>What we keep</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            From your sign-in with Microsoft or Google: the provider, your account id at that provider (subject),
            your name and e-mail address. Nothing else; no access tokens are stored.
        </li>
        <li>Your sandbox: generated data and the decisions you or the application make in it.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
        Only cookies needed to sign you in and to protect your forms: the sign-in session cookie, short-lived
        cookies used during the sign-in redirect, and an anti-forgery cookie. No analytics, no advertising.
    </p>
    <h2>Deletion</h2>
    <p>A sandbox that nobody used for 30 days is deleted with everything in it, including your name and e-mail.</p>
    <h2>AI</h2>
    <p>You never send text to an AI model. A scheduled job processes only generated data.</p>
</Shell>
